1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,085
You now have three lenses.

2
00:00:02,285 --> 00:00:04,078
P/E for profit.

3
00:00:04,278 --> 00:00:06,092
P/B for assets.

4
00:00:06,292 --> 00:00:09,322
EV to EBITDA for the whole business, debt included.

5
00:00:09,522 --> 00:00:11,378
No single one is the answer.

6
00:00:11,578 --> 00:00:13,504
The skill is reading them together.

7
00:00:14,254 --> 00:00:16,175
Check one: compare with peers.

8
00:00:16,375 --> 00:00:20,321
A P/E of thirty is normal for a fast-growing IT company,

9
00:00:20,321 --> 00:00:22,797
and alarming for a cement maker.

10
00:00:22,997 --> 00:00:26,347
A ratio only means something next to similar businesses.

11
00:00:27,097 --> 00:00:29,892
Check two: compare with the company's own history.

12
00:00:30,092 --> 00:00:33,446
If it usually trades at fifteen times earnings and is now

13
00:00:33,446 --> 00:00:35,597
at twenty-five, ask what changed.

14
00:00:35,797 --> 00:00:37,974
New growth, or just a hot market?

15
00:00:38,724 --> 00:00:41,498
Check three: look at the quality behind the number.

16
00:00:41,698 --> 00:00:43,402
Is return on equity high?

17
00:00:43,602 --> 00:00:44,649
Is debt low?

18
00:00:44,849 --> 00:00:48,007
Is the cash flow real, not just accounting profit?

19
00:00:48,207 --> 00:00:51,941
A cheap ratio on a bad business is a trap, not a bargain.

20
00:00:52,691 --> 00:00:54,174
A quick worked example.

21
00:00:54,374 --> 00:00:58,812
Company A: P/E twelve, P/B one, EV to EBITDA five.

22
00:00:59,012 --> 00:01:02,533
But return on equity six percent, and sales are shrinking.

23
00:01:02,733 --> 00:01:08,259
Company B: P/E twenty-five, P/B five, EV to EBITDA fourteen.

24
00:01:08,459 --> 00:01:10,571
Return on equity twenty-two percent,

25
00:01:10,571 --> 00:01:12,598
growing fifteen percent a year.

26
00:01:12,798 --> 00:01:13,891
A looks cheap.

27
00:01:14,091 --> 00:01:15,585
B looks expensive.

28
00:01:15,785 --> 00:01:18,120
Many great investors would pay up for B,

29
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:20,138
and many have been burned by A.

30
00:01:20,888 --> 00:01:24,451
So the ratio is the start of the conversation, not the end.

31
00:01:24,651 --> 00:01:26,752
The price tells you what the market thinks.

32
00:01:26,952 --> 00:01:29,035
The accounts tell you what the business is.

33
00:01:29,235 --> 00:01:32,307
Valuation is simply the habit of checking one against the

34
00:01:32,307 --> 00:01:34,612
other, before you hand over your money.

